{
  "dom_id": "step-q94193",
  "name": "Question 11",
  "problem": "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ compute $P(0.28<Z<1.82).$\n\n<table align=\"center\">\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"5\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr> <th width=\"25%\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$z$</th><th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.06\\,$</th><th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.07\\,$</th><th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.08\\,$</th>\n</tr><tr> <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.1\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.5636\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.5675\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.5714\\,$ </td></tr>\n<tr> <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.2\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.6026\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.6064\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.6103\\,$ </td></tr>\n<tr> <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.3\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.6406\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.6443\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.6480\\,$ </td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</th>\n\n<th width=\"5%\"></th>\n\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"5\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr> <th width=\"25%\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$z$</th><th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.00\\,$</th><th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.01\\,$</th><th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.02\\,$</th>\n</tr><tr> <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,1.7\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.9554\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.9564\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.9573\\,$ </td></tr>\n<tr> <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,1.8\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.9641\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.9649\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.9656\\,$ </td></tr>\n<tr> <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,1.9\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.9713\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.9719\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.9726\\,$ </td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</th>\n</tr>\n\n</tbody></table>",
  "worked_solution": "We're given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ and we wish to compute $P(0.28<Z<1.82).$ The required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14254773/assets/e50d6c8822357b7b8f21684e36133c91c2c6d541ab7f66951035eef5e9a239e6.png)\n\nBy the definition of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z),$ \n\n$$\nP(Z\\le z)=Φ(z).\n$$\n\nSo, we express the required probability in terms of $Φ(z)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(0.28<Z<1.82) & =P(Z<1.82)-P(Z\\le 0.28) \\\\  & =P(Z\\le 1.82)-P(Z\\le 0.28) \\\\  & =Φ(1.82)-Φ(0.28)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the tables, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(0.28) & =0.6103 \\\\ Φ(1.82) & =0.9656\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(0.28<Z<1.82) & =Φ(1.82)-Φ(0.28) \\\\  & =0.9656-0.6103 \\\\  & =0.3553.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
